  },
  "fixes": [
    "Align Python signed-key grammar with Rust DottedKey; reject invalid configuration before signing.",
    "Freeze independently resolved review route/hash/policy before new native uploads; reject stage-admission drift before material transfer.",
    "Preserve early unpinned policy readability and frozen query/cancel. New verification requires a complete pin and otherwise fails explicitly.",
    "Synchronize stale BYOK Goal test assertions with existing ordinary Agent semantics; no Goal production behavior changed."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Independent review parent/child, catalog commit and Agent consumption still require one continuous product-flow acceptance.",
    "No external model visual-quality or Office/WPS/Native-WASM acceptance in this stage.",
    "No deployment, platform distribution, performance or packaged-size claims.",
    "Strict Clippy passes six production Rust libraries. The full inherited sqlite_agent_loop test target still has 994 existing diagnostics; no lint suppression. New cross-process file has no diagnostics in the final check.",
    "Python regression has 294 existing deprecation warnings."
  ],
  "developmentFailures": [
    "Initial reused signer fixture had a Rust-incompatible numeric key segment; fixed at the Python validation source.",
    "Corrected owned model fixture constructor and its selected model class.",
    "Early cross-process flow used SQLite in the backend; final acceptance uses original PostgreSQL migrations.",
    "Minimal owned account table cannot load the full User ORM; supplied the explicit account-directory fixture port instead of claiming account provisioning coverage.",
    "Preserved all failed/interim command logs. Final functional reports match current source inventories."
  ],
